{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact 21341300c77c499e3a5b59c204ee7156de57760d. Two independent real CLI controls fail under race (evidence45d2d2d4, actual overlay and complete log attached). (1) Changing only the caller-selected target_ref from main to an existing other branch under the same key silently replays the accepted main request. restatePayloadTriple overwrites target_ref as well as generated fields before comparing signed bytes, erasing a meaningful caller-intent difference. Preserve and compare the selected ref and all other caller intent; only server-derived measurement may be recovered from the accepted event. The changed-intent call must refuse, never return a different destination's old request. (2) Deleting the branch after acceptance makes the identical retry fail during resolveRequestChoice before reproduceAcceptedTarget is reached. Resolve an authenticated exact accepted intent before a mutable-ref read; identical accepted retry must return its original event without a new append even if that ref is now absent, while a genuinely fresh missing-ref request must still refuse. Exercise both fixes through the common app boundary and actual CLI/MCP/HTTP plus guarded replacement routes; keep body/text/bases/attachments and ref-change disagreement controls and legacy exact retry. The author's moved-ref positive control passes; root's fresh missing-ref and explicit-empty-owner refusals also pass. Do not claim those prove the two missing cases.\nArchitecture: affected layers3/5/6/7 and their same-head architecture page are examined. Shared body-local ReadRequestChoice is a sound direction, but the promised immutable replay contract is violated and the new doc claim that an accepted retry measures nothing is false at this head. Update the implementation and any inaccurate contract text together. Security: caller-intent integrity fails when the requested destination is rewritten during replay; recovery also fails after ref deletion. These are blocking boundary defects. Simplification: keep one shared resolver and existing verified dedup path, distinguish caller-selected intent from generated measurement, and avoid a parallel retry cache or a compensating surface-only fix. Preserve original implementation request16cd3425 and promise07a271e5 for these same-outcome corrections, then publish the new exact head/artifacts for independent review. This verdict names the reporting artifact and examined core/CLI/MCP/architecture companions; the review stopped at these blockers and does not claim all49-file acceptance or full-suite verification.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:451ed4316a0f16d90b10a59db212f353a1484326","head":"21341300c77c499e3a5b59c204ee7156de57760d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e0086de0133dd44f43079569779c98774d7eeb89\",\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:45d2d2d4c3cd63eaa58bdcd835bbb95d3caf83a6\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:45d2d2d4c3cd63eaa58bdcd835bbb95d3caf83a6","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}